{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.18:1.1", "PA_thag_1.18:1.2"], "en": "“There was a monk, an heir of the Buddha, in the Bhesakaḷā Grove;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.18:1.3", "PA_thag_1.18:1.4"], "en": "Having pervaded this entire earth with the perception of a skeleton alone,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.18:1.5"], "en": "I think that he [has overcome] sensual lust.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.18:1.6"], "en": "“He will quickly cast it off.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.18:1.7"], "en": "… The Elder Siṅgālapitā … [said].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"}
